1200 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Now that we're back in London the people from the office are\helping me out, so things are way easier.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1210 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I had another dream last night. King Hroth was roaming a wasteland\with his people after being chased away from a neighboring country.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: It must have been the fault of the King of the North. This is\something that happens even now, where a stronger country will oppress\a weaker one.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1230 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: King Hroth claimed that God had abandoned him in favor of the King\of the North, and so he made an oath upon the star of darkness that he\would become the Devil King and sever the blood of the northern tribes...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1240 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: What's this star of darkness?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1250 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I have no idea. In my vision, King Hroth asked Susanna to inherit his\blood so that one day he'd get revenge upon the King of the North, no\mater how many years it would take.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: So this version of Susanna would carry on the legacy of King\Hroth, who looks just like you. I'm sure she must have loved him.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1270 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: That's where my vision stopped... You know how I've been having\nightmares? I feel like these visions have solved their mystery.":GOSUB 5100
1280 BM$="David: If what I've seen are real events from the past, then I may have\inherited the blood of King Hroth.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1290 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: But you're no Devil King, and there's no King of the North in our\world. Even if King Hroth was one of your ancestors, it would be from\countless generations ago. His power must be gone.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1300 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Maybe you're right. I don't have powers that would make me a Devil\King. Best I can do is have fancy dreams.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1310 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Yeah, don't worry about it anymore, or it might affect tonight's\concert. Speaking of which, it's getting late! I have to go. See you at the\venue.":GOSUB 5100
1320 BM$="After Susanna left, David tried to recall his nightmare, but he could only\remember some vague fragments. As he was starting to develop a\headache, he decided to stop thinking about it.":GOSUB 5100
1325 COMMON FO:BM$="David entered the lobby and had a cup of coffee to pass the time.":GOSUB 5100
1330 GOSUB 9010:GOSUB 6110:BM$="Eleno Vision was going to perform at the Royal Albert Hall. The seats were\already sold out for two days.":GOSUB 5100:'
1335 BM$="Though there were no tickets for sale that day, there were a lot of fans\gathered at the square.":GOSUB 5100
1340 GOSUB 6120:BM$="When the concert started, nobody left the square, listening to Eleno\Vision tapes with their earphones.":GOSUB 5100
1500 BM$="They may not have been able to get a seat, but they still wanted to stay\close to the stage and feel the heat of the band.":GOSUB 5100
1510 BM$="Even without hearing the actual performance, they were all sharing the\same purpose, silently receiving their energy.":GOSUB 5100
1520 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6130:BM$="However, it was nothing like the tremendous excitement currently\happening inside the concert hall.":GOSUB 5100
1590 GOSUB 6230:BM$="On top of the stage, David was singing with his usual energy. The crowd was\shouting so loudly that the walls themselves were shaking. It felt as if the\building itself could explode at any moment.":GOSUB 5100
1600 GOSUB 6200:BM$="David's energy excited the audience, and the audience's excitement\increased David's energy. They had already far surpassed most limits, and\yet no accidents occurred.":GOSUB 5100
1610 ISET X:GOSUB 6130:BM$="The critics would comment on the concert as such:\`Eleno Vision fills their audience with both excitement and reason, putting\them in a state that could only be called 'orderly euphoria'. It is no longer":GOSUB 5100:BM$="simply music, but something more. It is a religion.`":GOSUB 5100
1620 GOSUB 6220:BM$="Next to Susanna, President Richard started trembling with fear when he\saw the frenzied crowd, but then he was glad to see that his band was able\to keep the situation under control.":GOSUB 5100
1630 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6240:BM$="When the concert was over, Richard welcomed David and the others with a\sense of relief.":GOSUB 5100
1640 GOSUB 9020:GOSUB 6150:BM$="As they returned to their dressing rooms, Richard couldn't help but\praise them enthusiastically.":GOSUB 5100:'
