1900 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: You've been away only for a short period, but you've improved so\much, David! Same goes for the rest of you, you were amazing. Seriously,\what happened?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1910 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: I'd say it's all thanks to our fans overseas. They were so\enthusiastic about us that we had to improve to match their expectations.":GOSUB 5100
1920 BM$="Andrew: We had to become one with the audience.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1930 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: I've seen the way they get agitated, but somehow you're able to\use music to keep them under control. In all my years in this business I've\never seen anything like it.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1940 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: Come to think of it, there sure is a lot of people outside the venue.\Are you sure we've got enough security?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1950 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: I'm doubling security for your next concert. Don't worry, we'll\drive them away so they won't bother you.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1960 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: No, don't have them driven away, I feel like that's going to make the\situation worse. Nothing happened tonight, so let's just ignore them.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1970 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: I think we should have our next concert at the same place for an\entire week, so that everyone can listen to it. Plus, that'll make more\money for you.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1980 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Richard: That was actually my plan, but I couldn't make the reservation\this time.":GOSUB 5100
1990 BM$="At that moment, Susanna came in.":GOSUB 5100
2000 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Rather than focusing on making money, we should consider\making a world tour. Anyway, time to leave. There's a car waiting in the\back.":GOSUB 5100
2010 GOSUB 6160:BM$="Leaving from the back of the venue, the band took a car and returned to\their hotel.":GOSUB 5100
2020 BM$="After celebrating with a round of beers, they went back to their rooms to\recover from the concert.":GOSUB 5100
